<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">Limb I &middot; i &mdash; a sub-limb of Cosmic Physics</p>
  <h1>Astronomy: The Survey of the Sky</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">The oldest science and the only one whose laboratory cannot be entered. Everything
  on this page was worked out by sitting still, looking up, and being extremely careful about light.</p>
</section>

<!-- ============================== THE PREMISE ============================= -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--first illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">Begin Here</p>
    <h2 id="t-the-discipline-of-looking-up">The Discipline of Looking Up</h2>
    <p class="lede">Astronomy is the order's oldest limb and its strictest. It is where the mystical and the
    measurable have the longest shared border, and where the border is best policed.</p>

    <p>No astronomer has ever touched a star. Everything known about the composition, the mass, the age,
    the motion and the fate of every object beyond the solar system was extracted from light that arrived
    here on its own, was split into a spectrum, and was counted. That this works at all is one of the
    genuinely astonishing facts about the universe: matter everywhere emits and absorbs at the same
    frequencies as matter here, so a dark line in a star's spectrum names an element across ten billion
    years and ten billion light years. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span> established science.</p>

    <p>The order keeps astronomy and astrology in separate rooms on purpose. <a href="/astrology/">Astrology</a>
    is studied here as a symbolic technology with a real history and no predictive power over the physical;
    astronomy is the measurement. Both are honest work; confusing them is not.</p>

    <p class="muted small">Grading throughout: <span class="sci">&#9670; established science</span> &middot;
    <span class="hist">&#9670; scholarship and history</span> &middot;
    <span class="spec">&#9670; speculative and contested</span> &middot;
    <span class="myth">&#9670; myth, tradition and primary esoteric text</span>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

