<!-- ============================== THE STARS =============================== -->
<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">Limb I &middot; i &mdash; First Subject</p>
    <h2 id="t-what-a-star-is-and-which-kinds-there-are">What a Star Is, and Which Kinds There Are</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">A star is a ball of plasma in which gravity pulling in and radiation pushing out
    have agreed to a truce. The whole of stellar astronomy is the study of how that truce is kept, and how
    it ends.</p>
  </div>

  <figure id="fig-hr" class="plate">
    <figcaption class="plate-cap"><span class="plate-num">Plate I</span> The Hertzsprung&ndash;Russell Diagram
      <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></figcaption>
    <div class="plate-art">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 560 330" role="img" aria-label="A Hertzsprung-Russell diagram: temperature falling to the right, luminosity rising upward, with the main sequence running diagonally, giants above right and white dwarfs below left">
